@*
    The "Hitta hit" map on /kontakt. Drawn from OpenStreetMap data (the E 18 and AB 1031
    Åkerövägen roads, the coastline, and the property's position), simplified and exported
    once to path data — no external requests, no cookies, no map provider contacted when the
    page renders. NFR-35 forbids the embed outright: nothing may load from a third-party host
    while a page renders. It is also what makes §7 of the privacy policy true and keeps the
    site free of a consent banner, so replacing this with a provider iframe is never a purely
    visual decision.

    The SVG is *inline*, not behind an <img>. The logo lockups do the opposite (see design.md,
    Logo Variants) because <img> renders SVG sandboxed: no page CSS, no web fonts. Here that
    sandbox is exactly what we don't want — the map has to inherit the --color-* tokens and
    Roboto/Playfair from site.css, and its labels have to grow at the mobile breakpoint. Same
    fact about <img>, opposite conclusions, because the two graphics want opposite things.

    ODbL requires the map data to be credited; that happens in the figcaption rather than
    inside the drawing, so the credit is selectable text and its link can be followed.
*@

